{
  "body0": "Reduced to observables, the driver is this — prices around Atlas-Bridge I have tripled since the last safe-window season. In the record, Tau Reticuli Cohort appears as claimant and Tau Reticuli Service as incumbent; the field data is less tidy. One term in the system does not close: The compact between Tau Reticuli Cohort and Tau Reticuli Service fractured in the third pulse cycle. Three bodies define this problem: the failed terraforming biosphere, Catalog Authority, and Tau Reticuli Trust, which absorbs the perturbations. The boundary condition nobody can renegotiate: the insurers have quietly reclassified everything near Failed terraforming biosphere. Rebuild crews work the damaged ring under floodlights, around the clock, without press. The medical chirality stock versus Atlas-Bridge VII Station 18 is the headline; the secular decline in conditions at Atlas-Bridge II Station 88 is the data. Every model of the dispute shares one input: redundancy was cut three budgets ago and never restored. Salvage from the worst of it is still being sold with the serial numbers filed off. The dependency coefficient linking Atlas-Bridge II Station 88 to Medical chirality stock has grown every audit cycle since records began.",
  "spineEdgeType": "CONTESTS",
  "spineObjectKind": "namedFaction",
  "spineSubjectKind": "namedFaction",
  "spineSummary": "The compact between Tau Reticuli Cohort and Tau Reticuli Service broke in the third pulse cycle, the defining variable in this system is institutional: the two of them cannot agree on who certifies the numbers.",
  "spineVisibility": "contested",
}
`;

