{
  "body0": "New storage capacity gets built at triple redundancy and nobody calls it overreaction. The metric shear condensates presses, Mothallah Corridor-631 III Station 71 holds, and Mothallah Corridor-631 II Charter pays for both: wages frozen until someone blinks. Strip away the filings and the cause is plain — the supply contract renews on terms nobody has seen yet. Every shift change, someone repaints the boundary line around the metric shear condensates a hand-width farther out. The principals are the debt-fleet anchor graveyard and Mothallah Corridor-631 V; the casualty ledger, so far, is kept at Old navy depot. The pressure underneath is simple: the safety margins were drawn before Debt-fleet anchor graveyard started moving. The metric shear condensates wants first claim on the next harvest window; Mothallah Corridor-631 V - Moon I Claim guards the margin that keeps the lights on; Mothallah Corridor-631 II Charter gets a clinic that treats casualties from either camp and bills neither. The dispute runs at a simmer, and simmers out here have a way of finding fuel. One fact would reshuffle every position if it surfaced: the plague is industrial poisoning. The joint maintenance schedule still runs, but each side sends its own inspector to watch the other's. The ground lease under Old navy depot predates half the law that governs Mothallah Corridor-631 V. There, There is no second source for Metric shear condensates, and everyone at Mothallah Corridor-631 II Charter has done the math.",
  "spineEdgeType": "DEPENDS_ON",
